-- title:
--   Galois equivariance of the two degeneracy pull-backs on J₁(N)
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N$, $N'$, $t$ with $t \neq 0$, an index $i \in \{0,1\}$, a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and a class $x$ in [`ModularCurve.JOne N`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed level-$N$ $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionFieldBar N` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, degree-zero divisors modulo the subgroup of principal divisors. Here `degeneracyPullbackPair N N' t` is the pair of additive maps `JOne N →+ JOne N'` defined by case distinction on the predicate `DegeneracyPullbackInputs N N' t`, which asserts the existence of a divisibility $N t \mid N'$, of `HeckeBetaOneDefined N t`, of proofs that the two algebra maps `x1LevelInclBar` (the inclusion of the level-$N$ into the level-$N'$ base-changed function field, via $N \mid Nt \mid N'$) and `x1LevelSubstBar` (the composite of `heckeBetaOneBar`, the $q \mapsto q^t$ substitution, with `x1x0LevelInclBar`) are integral, of `HasPrincipalDivisors` for level $N'$, and of the fundamental identity along each of these two maps: when it holds, the two components are `Pic0.pullbackAlongHom` along those two maps, and otherwise both components are the zero map. The assertion is that the $i$-th component commutes with the action of $\sigma$ on the two divisor class groups: it sends $\sigma \cdot x$ to $\sigma \cdot$ (its value at $x$).
--
--   This records that the two degeneracy pull-backs $J_1(N) \to J_1(N')$, classically induced by $\tau \mapsto \tau$ and $\tau \mapsto t\tau$, are equivariant for the action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ acting coefficientwise on $q$-expansions, the degenerate convention making the statement unconditional. It is used in the analysis of the Galois module generated by the degeneracy maps on Tate modules of $J_1(N)$ that enters the level-lowering arguments.
